==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|balefull}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|bealofull}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbeɪl.fəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[portend|Portending]] [[evil]]; [[ominous]].
#* '''1674''', John Milton: ''[[w:Paradise Lost|Paradise Lost]] ''([[wikisource:Paradise Lost/Book I|Book I]])
#*: round he throws his '''baleful''' eyes, that witnessed huge affliction and dismay.
#* '''1873''', [[w:James Thomson (B.V.)|James Thomson (B.V.)]], ''[[s:The City of Dreadful Night|The City of Dreadful Night]]''
#*: The street-lamps burn amid the '''baleful''' glooms,
#*: Amidst the soundless solitudes immense
#*: Of ranged mansions dark and still as tombs.
#* '''1938''', [[w:Xavier Herbert|Xavier Herbert]], ''[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]'', New York: D. Appleton-Century, 1943, Chapter XII, p. 194, [https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb]
#*: {{...}} he went off alone with his family, and, watched by the day's red '''baleful''' eye, pumped the pump-car homeward, {{...}}
# Miserable, wretched, distressed, suffering.

